Before entering the hall, they smile and are prepared for the photographers where the official entourage awaits.
At the door of the hotel where they are accommodated, one of the four largest in the city, a reporter from Mexican television who likes to make jokes.
The best premium of fashion
Probably there was no more suitable place in the world than Paris to present a premium of fashion and there was probably no substantially excellent fashion designer and bon vivants than Valentino.
Mango presents the second edition of the ‘el Bóton-Mango Fashion Adwards’ fashion competition for the promotion and international increase of young fashion talents.
This is awarded with a cash prize of 300 000 euros.
Ayer Sandrina Fasoli, the Belgian winner of the first installment, saw her drawings yesterday in the shop window of the Mango branch on Boulevard Haussmann number 54 in Paris and almost cries because of the emotional excitement.
By the way, this is the second-largest shop of the company in Europe and was recently opened. It offers a sales area of 1 335 m2.
The biggest business is in London.
So many events have happened that are associated with thanking the fashion designer Valentino for his jury chairmanship at the competition. Everything ended with a luxury dinner at Opera National de Paris.
In the vicinity of many famous people, the board table organized by Mango seemed to be spectacular.
Nati, with the heavy heart shattered because because his brother recently died, tears himself up. He has put on the suit from the fashion house and haunted some jewelry from ELAH, which was breathtaking. He adhered to the arm of his son Luis, who is almost two meters tall and has accompanied Valentino at the dinner, in his honor.
Andik, the owner and gentleman of Mango House, greeted the guests and was such a cavalier, so that he ended together with the baron of Rotschild without jackets, because jackets they lent to the ladies.
Mónica Cruz, has rushed to the shop and had a pair of trousers and a shirt, which she modeled herself, and for dinner she wore a long, black sexy dress. During a night walk through the opera, accompanied by Goya Toledo, they showed us a hall for ballet rehearsals, so she got into excitement, remembered the old times, grabbed a bar and made a kind
Inés Sastre, did not join the walk through the premises of the palace, but before that she had shown us the photos of her son on the mobile phone.
The next morning we were able to look forward to the presence of Oliver Martínez, a personality who always provokes a stormy enthusiasm, and Jon Travolta, who after his arrival (with his own bedding lacquers and towels) at Hotel Internacional in Paris, asked in advance to have a room without smells.
The stars under the starlous sky of Paris
Oh la la, that's life.
1001 advice against stress
There is not 1000, but more a way to forget chaotic everyday life.
And even if there are few, everyone is collected in a book in which it says how to relax. The book comes into the bookshops on September 30.
The alarm clock is a punishment when it rings at 7 a.m., but even worse seems the notion of coming back into the hectic rhythm that current life demands.
The office is called the tension and the computer that leads to back pain.
Stress is the evil of the 21st century.
But there aren't one and not two methods to combat daily exhaustion and how to switch off from the world of work.
However, the number is rising, no more and no less than up to 1001.
In addition to yoga positions, classic massage or spa treatments, Susannah Marriott presents in the book the whole list of possibilities adapted to the tastes and time of each individual.
The work against the stress is called `1001 ways to relax' and so comes the tranquility that the book conveys, in the bookstores of the publishing house Pearson Alhambra and DK.
Anyone who thinks that it is impossible to achieve calm in areas such as workplace with the help of personal contacts, this manual refutes such faith.
In addition, the methods are offered, how to stay in contact with nature or suggest the 100% natural recipes that lead to relaxation.
If the adrenaline in your veins no longer rises to restore balance of the body and the stress has become a problem, so the moment has come to sit down on the sofa, turn off the brain and focus on reading.
Talking in your sleep
Some kids talk at night
I don’t mean those who wake up telling us something that happened the day before, but the children who speak during sleep.
If it happens to you for the first time, at best you'll be terrified, but in reality that has no meaning.
This is a positive sleep disorder called speaking during sleep.
It is quite common, especially among children and adolescents.
Surely, more than one of you was told that you spoke at night.
This phenomenon can occur occasionally (once in a lifetime, for example, such as during high fever), or regularly (every day, once a week, once a month), the next day the child cannot remember anything.
There is nothing reason that causes this phenomenon.
Often connections are sought with other appearances in sleep, such as nightmares, panicked anxiety at night, Enuresis noctura (bedwetting at night), talking in sleep, but there is no reason for it.
As we’ve mentioned earlier, it can be due to very high fiber, stress situations, or overwhelm.
In any case, that's a little-studied phenomenon.
The frequency with which it occurs is very variable.
It may be that one speaks quietly in individual words, whispers or it can be quite the opposite (screams, crying, long discussions).
In cases, if the utterance is very intense, it is recommended to observe the child and get advice from a specialist to check whether there is a problem that causes anxiety and occurs in this way.
We’ve said it’s a positive disorder, so it doesn’t get treated, be it, it’s associated with another sleep disorder that can be treated (for example, with sleep apnea, or stress).
What can be done is carry out a series of simple preventive measures:
Don't try to excite the child before sleeping.
So, choose quiet play for the child and avoid stressful television programs that are terrible and a bit too wild.
In the nervous children who are recommended for relaxation, relaxation methods can be used to help them get some inner rest.
It helps the kid to sleep peacefully.
If speaking in your sleep occurs, try to keep calm.
Remember that it’s harmless for the child and the next day it won’t be able to remember anything that happened.
Beneficial advice
Don't wake it up.
This is useless, because the child is unconscious, so you will take him out of sleep.
Even the child speaks, he sleeps, so he rests.
Remember, if it is scared after a pair of apparitions, it is recommended to seek advice or to find out what reason the child has for fear.
If they understand what it says (which isn’t so ordinary), the child doesn’t put pressure to conduct an interrogation and get more information.
So you won't be able to achieve anything because when the child sleeps, he is unconscious and can't think about it.
In addition, you will hear what it says, but you will not know what it dreams and why it says it, therefore they are careful with the interpretation of the information and the conclusions you draw from it.
Maybe, it doesn't tell the kind that you hear that at night and know its secrets.
Not even as a joke.
It causes a lot of fear.
So, don't worry, it's nothing bad, that's a moment that lasts just a few minutes.
Ill houses ... finally
After a long stretch of thirst, Illhäuser is finally back on track for success on the pitch.
Without much effort, the yellow-blacks scored numerous goal chances and managed to implement one of them, and thus win the game.
The pace of this encounter, in which the attackers struggled to shower their skills, wasn't very high.
After a first attack by guest captain Kauffmann, whose long-range shot went narrowly past the angle, Illhäuser was supposed to dominate the game with ease, and it alternately succeeded to challenge Denmark's defense with a long-range shot, then brain with a high-pass, and Romain with a shot with the tip of his foot.
The opposing squad blocked in the middle of the field, leaving only the lively Riahi at the top of the storm through.
The beginning of the second half should be decisive with initially two goal chances won by Riahi and Temporale, and immediately afterwards with the first goal for the Illhäuser by Marais, who stood just right to accept a ball that had been fended off by Diebold in a first attempt.
But the Illhäusian goalscorer should not be able to enjoy his luck for long and be sent to the bench about twelve minutes later, whereby his team-mates had to continue to play numerically outnumbered.
Denmark, however, didn't know how to take advantage of this and didn't confront an Illhaeusian eleven, which withdrewed just a bit to 'condense' their defence, except in the very last seconds of the game in which the ball passed very close to the slat after a big squabble.
Sarkozy meets angry fishermen
Before flying to the United States Nicolas Sarkozy will make another detour to Brittany.
In view of the determined attitude of the fishermen, who blocked access to several Breton and Norman ports on Monday, the French president decided to gather in the port of Guilvinec at the Finistère on Tuesday morning to meet their representatives there.
The latter promised to receive him `with a constructive spirit', and hope that he comes with 'concrete proposals'.
The visit of the President takes place at the same time as a general meeting of the crisis committee established by the Breton fishermen to enforce measures in view of the extreme increase in the price of diesel, which has reached a record value of an average of over 1.14 euros per liter.
According to Elysee Palace spokesman David Martinon `the president will discuss with them possible solutions to help their companies become competitive again, and to secure workplace conditions and seafarers' paid."
Sarkozy is expected with determination by the fishermen.
Tuesday morning they led protest marches in the Morbihan and Calvados, which caused traffic jams of almost ten kilometers in length.
Quiberon's sailing port was also blocked, but the ties to Belle-île did not break off.
Quiberon Peninsula has been delineated with a barrier.
As early as Monday, the sailors expressed their determination by burning tires and pallets from the early morning in front of the fuel depots of the ports of Brest and Lorient, while demonstrations were held in Concarneau or Saint-Brieuc.
The movement spread to other ports on the Atlantic coast and the English Channel, such as Sables d'Olonnes, in Vendée, where the fishing boats didn't go out, or Le Havre, where about twenty boats blocked the manoeuvres of the merchant ships.
The fishermen of Turballe and Croisic in Loire-Atlantique broke up the blockade of the important total refinery in Donges in the evening.
Those from Boulogne-sur-Mer decided to await the course of Wednesday's meeting at the ministry before deciding on possible measures.
In fact, the crisis committee in Guilvinec has to decide on the reactions to the movement and its participation in the discussion planned at the Ministry of Agriculture and Fisheries in Paris.
But some Bretonian fishermen don't want to be represented by those in charge of the national fisheries committee that has not supported their movement.
`The strike will continue', because 'the fishermen will not give in at any point' and `don't want to go to Paris,' announced Liliane Cariou, president of Lorient's fisheries committee.
The professional fishermen, who do not pay taxes on diesel, the liter currently costs about 50 cents, but they think that the profitability limit of a boat can only be reached with diesel for less than 30 cents per liter.
